  "description": "One notification family for inline feedback and floating messages. Inline notifications use a semantic outline with no background fill; floating notifications use a neutral surface. Use `action` for a labeled callback, `actions` for custom controls, and `onDismiss` for a dismiss button. The floating variant styles the message; `NotificationViewport` and `showNotification` place it above the application.\n\nMount one `NotificationViewport` per application shell, then call `showNotification`. Its action callback also dismisses that message. Loading notifications stay visible until replaced or dismissed; other notifications default to 5 seconds. `Banner`/`Callout` and `Toast`/`Toaster`/`showToast` remain compatibility APIs for the same family.\n\n| NotificationViewport prop | Type | Default / behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| position | top-left, top-center, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-center, bottom-right | bottom-right |\n| offset | number, string, or side-offset object | 12 |\n| gap | number | 12 |\n| visibleToasts | number | 4 |\n| duration | number | Sonner host timeout in milliseconds; individual calls may override it |\n| theme | light, dark, system | Optional host appearance; message content uses Aegis theme tokens |\n| expand / closeButton | boolean | Expand the stack / show a host close control |\n| hotkey | string[] | Keyboard shortcut that focuses the notification region |\n| containerAriaLabel | string | Accessible name for the notification region |\n| toastOptions | ToastOptions | Shared host settings; Aegis unstyled content remains enabled |\n| className / style | string / CSSProperties | Host presentation props |",
  "exports": [
    "Notification",
    "NotificationViewport"
  ],
  "importStatements": [
    "import { Notification, NotificationViewport } from '@dimitriszoitas/aegis-ui/notification';"
  ],
  "stylesheetImport": "import '@dimitriszoitas/aegis-ui/styles.css';",
